request.description:
Outcome: the task store guarantees "column field == column folder", so listing, moving and archiving a card can never disagree.

Test to add (one increment, no production change unless the test proves a bug):
1. create a task through `TaskManager.create_task(board="IT team", column="Backlog")` in a temporary project;
2. assert `.codx/tasks/IT team/Backlog/<slug>.<id>.json` exists and its JSON `column` is `Backlog`;
3. move it to `Doing` and assert the file was relocated (one file only, none left in `Backlog`) and `column`/`status_history` are updated;
4. archive and restore it and assert it comes back to `Doing`.

Acceptance evidence: `pytest -k task_move` (or the file's own module path) green, output pasted in the card, plus the diff of any production fix the test forces.

Owner: qa_automation. Reference: `api/codx/junior/task_manager.py`, `docs/features/kanban.md` (storage layout + archive section).

Outcome: `docs/features/autonomous-agents.md` explains what a coworker does with a card, so the rules are not only in the prompt.

Content to add (short section, ~15 lines):
- one card = one increment; never widen the scope of the card;
- when the increment is done the actor comments with the changed files and the validation command + result;
- the actor then moves the card to `Review`; the author never closes its own card, `reviewer` does;
- anything that must be checked later becomes a task with `wake_at` (cross-link to the `wake_at` section);
- if the destination column and the file folder can disagree, document the expected behaviour or reference the fix card.

Acceptance evidence: new/edited section in `docs/features/autonomous-agents.md` (paste the heading and a permalink-style path), plus one inbound link from `docs/features/kanban.md` (Board manager / Tasks are chats) so the rule is reachable from the kanban docs.

Owner: wiki.

